14n1|v|To perceive or apprehend clearly and certainly; to understand; to have full information of; as, to know one's duty. ; To be convinced of the truth of; to be fully assured of; as, to know things from information. ; To be acquainted with; to be no stranger to; to be more or less familiar with the person, character, etc., of; to possess experience of; as, to know an author; to know the rules of an organization. ; To recognize; to distinguish; to discern the character of; as, to know a person's face or figure. ; To have sexual commerce with. ; To have knowledge; to have a clear and certain perception; to possess wisdom, instruction, or information; -- often with of. ; To be assured; to feel confident.	d:1cdu,27,6;2cf,26,7;x5,17,5;1oar,13,6;psk,12,8~psk,12,8;2cf,26,7;1cdu,27,6;1oar,13,6;x5,17,5	D:pwk,40,7~pwk,40,7
